-- title:
--   Fractions over a subfield of constants at a place
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $N$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid N$, and $k$ a field of characteristic $q$. Write $F = \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,N$ for the subfield of the Laurent series field $k((\mathfrak q))$ generated over $k$ by the two series $\mathrm{jqModC}\,k$ (the $\mathfrak q$-expansion $\mathfrak q^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{jNum}$ read in $k$) and its $N$-fold substitute $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k\,N = \mathrm{qExpand}\,k\,N(\mathrm{jqModC}\,k)$; denote by $\tilde\jmath = \mathrm{jGeomGen}\,k\,N$ and $\tilde\jmath_N = \mathrm{jNGeomGen}\,k\,N$ the corresponding elements of $F$. Let $k_0$ be a subfield of $k$, and let $v$ be a place of $F$ over $k$, that is, a valuation subring $\mathcal O_v \subsetneq F$ containing $k$ and which is a principal ideal ring. Assume $\tilde\jmath \in \mathcal O_v$, and let $f \in F$ lie both in $\mathcal O_v$ and in the subfield of $F$ generated by the image of $k_0$ together with $\tilde\jmath$ and $\tilde\jmath_N$. Then there are $a, s \in F$, each integral over the $k$-subalgebra $k[\tilde\jmath,\tilde\jmath_N]$, each lying in that same subfield generated by $k_0$, $\tilde\jmath$, $\tilde\jmath_N$, and each having all Laurent coefficients (at every index $n \in \mathbb Z$) in $k_0$, such that $s \neq 0$, both $s$ and $s^{-1}$ lie in $\mathcal O_v$, and $f s = a$.
--
--   This is the statement that a $v$-regular function rational over the subfield of constants $k_0$ can be written as a quotient of two $k_0$-rational functions integral over $k[\tilde\jmath,\tilde\jmath_N]$ whose denominator is a unit at $v$; concretely, $\mathcal O_v \cap k_0(\tilde\jmath,\tilde\jmath_N)$ is a localisation of the integral closure of $k_0[\tilde\jmath]$ in $k_0(\tilde\jmath,\tilde\jmath_N)$. It is used in the analysis of residues at nodes of the special fibre, in the two saturation results [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.nodeResidue_saturated_of_orderLawFixed`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.nodeResidue_saturated_of_orderLawFixed) and its Noetherian variant.
